# sent_id = urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0012.tlg001.perseus-grc2:1.33.4
# text = κλῦθί μευ ἀργυρότοξʼ, ὃς Χρύσην ἀμφιβέβηκας Κίλλαν τε ζαθέην Τενέδοιό τε ἶφι ἀνάσσεις, Σμινθεῦ εἴ ποτέ τοι χαρίεντʼ ἐπὶ νηὸν ἔρεψα, ἢ εἰ δή ποτέ τοι κατὰ πίονα μηρίʼ ἔκηα ταύρων ἠδʼ αἰγῶν, τὸ δέ μοι κρήηνον ἐέλδωρ·
# sentence_id = 17
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Hear me, lord of the silver bow, you who guard Chrysa and holy Cilla and rule Tenedos with might, Smintheus! If ever I roofed a pleasing temple for you, or if ever I burned the fat thigh-bones of bulls and goats to you, fulfill this wish for me:
# literal_translation = Hear me, silver-bowed one, who Chrysa have-stood-around, and Cilla the holy, and of-Tenedos with-might you-rule, Smintheus, if ever for-you a pleasing temple I-roofed, or if indeed ever for-you down the fat thigh-pieces I-burned of-bulls and of-goats, this for-me fulfill, [my] wish:
