# sent_id = urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0012.tlg001.perseus-grc2:1.68.2
# text = τοῖσι δʼ ἀνέστη Κάλχας Θεστορίδης οἰωνοπόλων ὄχʼ ἄριστος, ὃς ᾔδη τά τʼ ἐόντα τά τʼ ἐσσόμενα πρό τʼ ἐόντα, καὶ νήεσσʼ ἡγήσατʼ Ἀχαιῶν Ἴλιον εἴσω ἣν διὰ μαντοσύνην, τήν οἱ πόρε Φοῖβος Ἀπόλλων·
# sentence_id = 33
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Among them rose Calchas son of Thestor, far the best of bird-diviners, who knew the things that are, the things to come, and the things that had been before, and who had guided the ships of the Achaeans to Ilium by the gift of prophecy that Phoebus Apollo had given him.
# literal_translation = Among them rose Calchas Thestorides, of bird-diviners far the best, who knew the things being and the things about-to-be and the things being before, and [who] led the ships of-the-Achaeans into Ilium by his prophetic-art, which to-him gave Phoebus Apollo.
