# sent_id = urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0012.tlg001.perseus-grc2:1.92.2
# text = οὔ τʼ ἄρ ὅ γʼ εὐχωλῆς ἐπιμέμφεται οὐδʼ ἑκατόμβης, ἀλλʼ ἕνεκʼ ἀρητῆρος ὃν ἠτίμησʼ Ἀγαμέμνων, οὐδʼ ἀπέλυσε θύγατρα καὶ οὐκ ἀπεδέξατʼ ἄποινα, τοὔνεκʼ ἄρʼ ἄλγεʼ ἔδωκεν ἑκηβόλος ἠδʼ ἔτι δώσει·
# sentence_id = 46
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = It is not, then, over a vow or a hecatomb that he is aggrieved, but because of the priest whom Agamemnon dishonored, and did not release his daughter nor accept the ransom—therefore the Far-shooter gave us griefs, and will yet give more.
# literal_translation = Not, then, [is] he at all aggrieved on account of a vow nor of a hecatomb, but on account of the priest whom Agamemnon dishonored, and did not release [his] daughter and did not accept ransoms, for that reason indeed the Far-shooter gave griefs and still will give [them].
