# sent_id = urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0012.tlg001.perseus-grc2:1.92.3
# text = οὐδʼ ὅ γε πρὶν Δαναοῖσιν ἀεικέα λοιγὸν ἀπώσει πρίν γʼ ἀπὸ πατρὶ φίλῳ δόμεναι ἑλικώπιδα κούρην ἀπριάτην ἀνάποινον, ἄγειν θʼ ἱερὴν ἑκατόμβην ἐς Χρύσην·
# sentence_id = 47
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Nor will he drive wretched destruction from the Danaans until he gives back to her dear father the bright-eyed girl without price or ransom, and leads the sacred hecatomb to Chryse.
# literal_translation = Nor will he at all before drive away for the Danaans shameful destruction, before [he] give back to [her] dear father the bright-eyed girl unbought, unransomed, and lead a sacred hecatomb to Chryse.
