# sent_id = urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0012.tlg001.perseus-grc2:1.92.11
# text = καὶ νῦν ἐν Δαναοῖσι θεοπροπέων ἀγορεύεις ὡς δὴ τοῦδʼ ἕνεκά σφιν ἑκηβόλος ἄλγεα τεύχει, οὕνεκʼ ἐγὼ κούρης Χρυσηΐδος ἀγλάʼ ἄποινα οὐκ ἔθελον δέξασθαι, ἐπεὶ πολὺ βούλομαι αὐτὴν οἴκοι ἔχειν·
# sentence_id = 55
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = And now you stand among the Danaans prophesying that the archer god is causing them pains for this reason, because I was unwilling to accept the splendid ransom for the girl Chryseis, since I much prefer to keep her at home.
# literal_translation = And now among the Danaans, prophesying, you declare that indeed on account of this the far-shooter is making pains for them, because I was not willing to receive the splendid ransoms of the girl Chryseis, since I much prefer to have her herself at home.
