# text = εἷς δέ τις ἀρχὸς ἀνὴρ βουληφόρος ἔστω, ἢ Αἴας ἢ Ἰδομενεὺς ἢ δῖος Ὀδυσσεὺς ἠὲ σὺ Πηλεΐδη πάντων ἐκπαγλότατʼ ἀνδρῶν, ὄφρʼ ἥμιν ἑκάεργον ἱλάσσεαι ἱερὰ ῥέξας.
# sentence_id = 74
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Let some one man be our leader and counselor — either Ajax, or Idomeneus, or godlike Odysseus, or you, son of Peleus, most formidable of all men — so that you may appease the god who strikes from afar by performing sacred rites for us.
# literal_translation = But let some one man be leader, a counsel-bearing man, either Ajax or Idomeneus or godlike Odysseus or you, son of Peleus, most formidable of all men, so that for us you may propitiate the one who works from afar, having performed sacred rites.
