# text = οὐ γὰρ πώποτʼ ἐμὰς βοῦς ἤλασαν οὐδὲ μὲν ἵππους, οὐδέ ποτʼ ἐν Φθίῃ ἐριβώλακι βωτιανείρῃ καρπὸν ἐδηλήσαντʼ, ἐπεὶ ἦ μάλα πολλὰ μεταξὺ οὔρεά τε σκιόεντα θάλασσά τε ἠχήεσσα·
# sentence_id = 78
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = For they never once drove off my cattle or my horses, nor ever in deep-soiled, man-nourishing Phthia did they ravage the harvest, since truly there lies between us much — shadowy mountains and the resounding sea.
# literal_translation = For not ever yet did they drive off my cattle, nor indeed my horses, nor ever in Phthia of the rich soil, nurse of men, did they damage the harvest, since truly very many [things lie] between — both shadowy mountains and the resounding sea.
