# sent_id = urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0012.tlg001.perseus-grc2:1.172.9
# text = ὡς ἔμʼ ἀφαιρεῖται Χρυσηΐδα Φοῖβος Ἀπόλλων, τὴν μὲν ἐγὼ σὺν νηΐ τʼ ἐμῇ καὶ ἐμοῖς ἑτάροισι πέμψω, ἐγὼ δέ κʼ ἄγω Βρισηΐδα καλλιπάρῃον αὐτὸς ἰὼν κλισίην δὲ τὸ σὸν γέρας ὄφρʼ ἐῢ εἰδῇς ὅσσον φέρτερός εἰμι σέθεν, στυγέῃ δὲ καὶ ἄλλος ἶσον ἐμοὶ φάσθαι καὶ ὁμοιωθήμεναι ἄντην.
# sentence_id = 94
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Since Phoebus Apollo is taking Chryseis from me, her I will send away with my ship and my companions, but I myself will go and take fair-cheeked Briseis, your prize, from your hut, so that you may know well how much mightier I am than you, and that another man may dread to speak as my equal and to compare himself to me to my face.
# literal_translation = As Phoebus Apollo takes away from me Chryseis, her indeed I will send with my ship and with my companions, but I, I will lead away beautiful-cheeked Briseis, going myself to [your] hut, your prize, so that you may know well how much mightier I am than you, and [so that] another also may dread to say [himself] equal to me and to be made like [me] face to face.
