# sent_id = urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0012.tlg001.perseus-grc2:1.172.11
# text = Πηλεΐωνι δʼ ἄχος γένετʼ, ἐν δέ οἱ ἦτορ στήθεσσιν λασίοισι διάνδιχα μερμήριξεν, ἢ ὅ γε φάσγανον ὀξὺ ἐρυσσάμενος παρὰ μηροῦ τοὺς μὲν ἀναστήσειεν, ὃ δʼ Ἀτρεΐδην ἐναρίζοι, ἦε χόλον παύσειεν ἐρητύσειέ τε θυμόν.
# sentence_id = 96
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Grief came upon the son of Peleus, and within his breast his heart pondered two ways: whether to draw the sharp sword from beside his thigh, make the others get up, and kill the son of Atreus, or to check his anger and restrain his spirit.
# literal_translation = To-the-son-of-Peleus grief came, and in [to] him [his] heart in [his] shaggy breast pondered in-two-ways, whether he, having drawn the sharp sword from beside [his] thigh, should make the others get up, and he should slay the son of Atreus, or should stop [his] anger and should restrain [his] spirit.
